  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**\n\nCore Idea:  \nImplement a structured optimization approach combining **Bayesian optimization** for adaptive dataset selection with **deep reinforcement learning** (specifically, deep deterministic policy gradient - DDPG) to control the step-function with multilevel constraints.\n\nKey Motivation:  \nThe previous method struggled to escape local optima by restricting itself to gradient-based improvements within fixed representations. This new approach breaks that constraint:  \n- First identify a minimal set of training signals through Bayesian optimization analysis  \n- Then deploy a gradient-free optimization framework (DDPG) to explore while preserving constraints  \n- Finally embed a local polishing phase using randomized rounding and projection to achieve robustness\n\nBottleneck Addressed:  \nTrapped in the continuous space optimization with crisp constraints. Broken into  \n1. Signal selection (low-resolution info gathering)  \n2. Generic exploration (high-dimensional action space)  \n3. Final refinement (discrete support extraction)\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**\n\n**Variables:**  \nLet \\( h: [0,2] \\to [0,1] \\) with integral constraint \\(\\int_0^2 h(x) dx = 1\\).  \nDiscrete representation: \\( h \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n} \\) with \\( \\text{sum}(h) = n/2 \\).\n\n**Objective:**  \n\\(\\min_h \\max_k \\int_0^2 h(x) \\cdot (1 - h(x+k)) dx\\)  \n=> \\(\\min_h \\text{smoothmax}_{ \\beta}\\left\\{ \\text{correlation}(h, 1-h) \\right\\}\\)\n\n**Derived Functions:**  \n- **Correlation Kernel:** \\( c(k) = \\text{integral overlap between h and } 1-h \\text{ at shift } k \\)\n- **Smoothmax:** Functional approximation for \\( \\max_k c(k) \\) with derivative needed for DDPG\n\n**Constraints:**\n- Bounded components: \\( 0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1 \\)\n- Integral preservation: \\( \\sum h_i \\approx n/2 \\)\n- (To be enforced via projection)\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**\n\nParent Transfer:  \nIf initial_h_values provided, sample kernel from it via Gaussian smoothing.\n\nPhase 0: Dataset Selection  \n- Use Bayesian Optimization to determine minimal signals needed for exploration  \n  \u2022 Score function: indicative approximation performance vs. signal variance  \n  \u2022 Search across possible (noisy shift) configurations\n\nPhase 1: DDPG-Based Policy  \n- State: current \\( h + perturbation \\) (real space)  \n- Action: how much to change \\( h \\) (but preserve integral)  \n- Reward: -smoothmax_correlation\n- Use priority experience replay\n\nCode Outline:\n\ndef project_feasible(h):\n  # FastL1 projection onto simplex-constraint surface\n\nclass DDPGAgent:\n  def __init__(self, state_size, action_size):\n    self.actor = ActorNetwork(state_size, action_size)\n    self.critic = CriticNetwork(state_size, action_size)\n    # Use Adam optimizers\n\ndef compute_smoothmax(h):\n  # Avoids over-max noise penalties\n\ndef evaluate_state(h):\n  # Fast approximation with projection\n\nPhase 2: Local Adaptive Rounding\n  \u2022 Randomly sample $m$ segments to activate/deactivate  \n  \u2022 Reevaluate after rounding constraint-based\n\n4. **Search Choices and Variations**\n\nCore Configuration:\n- Phase 1: Active noise \\( \\sigma = [0.8,0.3] \\) decreasing by \\( \\alpha=0.15 \\)\n- Phase 2: Round-window size \\( m \\in [3,7] \\) tuned by prior failures\n\nKey Variants:\n1. **Adaptive Noise-aware Momentum** (val_ARCH): modifies exploration based on gradient trace\n2. **Shift-invariant Term** (val_SIT): adds feature to keep h near its moving average\n3. **Greedy Sticking** (val_GS): enables worst-candidate escape\n\nTriggered under:\n- Poor exploration rate (var_ARCH > 0.7)\n- Slow convergence (|\\Delta smoothmax| < 2^-4 over 100 steps)\n\n5. **Compute Budget and Robustness**\n\nFixed time budget 1100s:\n- 400s: Phase 0 Dataset selection\n- 500s: Bayesian/UCB shaping\n- 200s: DDPG training (\u223c5e4 samples)\n- 100s: Final rounding + verification\n- 100s: Contingent retraining if local minima suspected\n\nProtection against:\n- Infinite loops: step-size limits + timeout\n- Invalid states: projection guarantees feasible points\n- Nans: clipping gradients at value 3\n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**\n\nOutput post-processing:\n1. Check feasibility: |sum(h) - n/2| < 1e-4\n2. Forced re-projection if failed\n3. at least 3 independent evaluation samples\n4. Score = max(0.3808, C_5) \n\nFinal structural guarantees:\n- All outputs in [0,1]^n\n- Dimension n=200 (default) \n- Prior knowledge inject method (notably if extremes found)",
